---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About Dr. DuBose · DuBose, M.D." active="about">

  <!-- 1 · Introduction -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-block:clamp(56px,8vw,96px)">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="photo-frame">
          <div class="photo" style="aspect-ratio:4/5">
            <img src="/images/dr-dubose.jpg" alt="Dr. Logan DuBose" width="800" height="1000" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <span class="eyebrow">About me</span>
          <h1 style="font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,44px)">Logan DuBose, M.D.</h1>
          <p style="margin-top:20px">
            I&rsquo;m a doctor and researcher. I practice primary care and
            lead research on aging, caregiving, and health technology.
            This practice brings the two together: one doctor, a small
            panel, and enough time to do medicine well.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · My path -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The path</span>
          <h2>Why I practice this way</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I earned my M.D. at the Texas A&amp;M College of Medicine and
            completed an internal medicine internship at George
            Washington University. Then I took an unusual path. Instead of
            the standard hospital track, I became the research lead for
            NIH-funded studies on aging, caregiving, and digital health
            tools. The whole time, I kept practicing primary care,
            including as a volunteer physician at a charity clinic.
          </p>
          <p>
            That work taught me a simple lesson. Most people are not
            failed by a lack of medicine. They are failed by
            fragmentation: fifteen-minute visits, results with no
            explanation, five doctors and no one holding the whole
            picture.
          </p>
          <p>
            This practice is my answer. One doctor and one patient, with
            enough time between them. I keep the panel small and the
            overhead low, so the price stays at $100 a month and visits
            last as long as they need. I still lead research on healthy
            aging. Each job makes me better at the other.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · Training and credentials -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The record</span>
          <h2>Training and credentials</h2>
          <p style="margin-top:18px"><a class="quiet" href="/cv">Read my full CV &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row"><b>M.D.</b><p>Texas A&amp;M College of Medicine</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Internship</b><p>Internal medicine, George Washington University</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Licensure</b><p>Virginia (unrestricted), DEA-registered; Texas licensure [at launch]</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Clinical practice</b><p>Part-time primary care; volunteer general practitioner, Fredericksburg Christian Health Center</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Research</b><p>Chief Research Officer, Olera; research lead on NIH-funded studies of aging, caregiving, and health technology; Affiliate Faculty, Texas A&amp;M School of Public Health, Center for Community Health &amp; Aging</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>In progress</b><p>Lifestyle medicine certification, International Board of Lifestyle Medicine</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Education</b><p>B.S. Biochemistry, The University of Texas at Austin; M.B.A., Texas A&amp;M University</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · Selected research -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Research</span>
          <h2>Selected research</h2>
          <p style="margin-top:14px" class="soft">
            My research covers aging, caregiving, access to care, and
            health technology. A few representative publications:
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pubs">
          <p class="pub">
            <b>Development and Evaluation of a Web-Based Platform for
            Dementia Caregivers</b>
            DuBose L, et al. JMIR Research Protocols. 2024.
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.2196/64127">doi:10.2196/64127</a>
          </p>
          <p class="pub">
            <b>Financial, Legal, and Functional Challenges of Caring for
            People Living With Dementia</b>
            Fan Q, DuBose L (co-first author), et al. JMIR Aging. 2023.
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.2196/47577">doi:10.2196/47577</a>
          </p>
          <p class="pub">
            <b>The Olera.care Digital Caregiving Assistance Platform:
            Preliminary Evaluation</b>
            Fan Q, Hoang MN, DuBose L, et al. JMIR Aging. 2024.
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.2196/55132">doi:10.2196/55132</a>
          </p>
          <p class="pub">
            <b>Understanding Older Adults&rsquo; Perceptions of AI Use in
            Financial Decisions</b>
            Allahvirdi S, et al; DuBose L, senior author. Human Factors
            in Aging and Special Needs. 2025.
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.54941/ahfe1006290">doi:10.54941/ahfe1006290</a>
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:20px">
            <a class="quiet" href="/cv">Full publication list in my CV &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · How I practice -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Commitments</span>
          <h2>How I practice</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Evidence first</b>
          <p>I recommend what good evidence supports. When the evidence
          is thin or mixed, I say so.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>I explain my reasoning</b>
          <p>You will know what I recommend and why.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>I say &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t know&rdquo; when I don&rsquo;t</b>
          <p>Then I find out, or I find the person who knows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>I refer without ego</b>
          <p>When someone else is the right doctor for part of your care,
          you&rsquo;ll be in their office, with me still watching the
          whole picture.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Your decisions are yours</b>
          <p>My job is to make sure they are informed and unrushed.</p>
        </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · Outside the practice -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Off the clock</span>
          <h2>Outside the practice</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I&rsquo;m married to a pediatrician I met in medical school. I
            play jazz, read, and write. My wife and I travel, go to live
            comedy, and get to the beach when we can. Some of the most
            meaningful medicine I&rsquo;ve done has been on medical
            mission trips. They taught me how much a doctor can do with
            little besides time and attention.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>The best way to know if we&rsquo;d work well together is to talk.</h2>
        <p>Thirty minutes by video, free. If I&rsquo;m not the right fit,
        I&rsquo;ll say so and point you toward someone good.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
